# Cloudflare Pages serves these headers with the static assets. The function
# plane (`/api/*`, `/user/*`) is not affected by this file.
#
# The widget sandbox's synchronous query bridge is a SharedArrayBuffer, so the
# document must be cross-origin isolated. Every asset the shell loads is
# same-origin, and the Cloudflare Access round-trip is a top-level navigation,
# which COOP `same-origin` does not block. Keep the three headers together:
# without them the sandbox cannot boot and widget bubbles fall back to a card.

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin

# The service worker decides which build the browser runs, so it must be
# re-checked on every load. The hashed assets it points at never change, so
# they are cached forever.
/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/manifest.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
